# Shell scripts under poc/linux-client-test/ run INSIDE WSL2/Ubuntu (Linux) -
# force LF line endings regardless of the checkout platform or any local
# core.autocrlf setting, so a Windows checkout never silently reintroduces
# CRLF (which breaks `#!/usr/bin/env bash` shebangs and confuses bash).
poc/linux-client-test/*.sh eol=lf

# Same rationale, extended to vault-dns (WP 1.8): functional-check.sh runs
# INSIDE WSL2/Linux (shebang breaks under CRLF same as above), and
# dnsmasq.conf.template is envsubst'd verbatim inside a Linux container
# (WP 1.9) -- a CRLF checkout would bake a trailing \r into every
# substituted line (e.g. address=.../CACHE_IP\r), which dnsmasq's parser
# does not tolerate and would fail to start on, not just a cosmetic issue.
dns/tests/*.sh eol=lf
dns/*.template eol=lf
